---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro'

export const prerender = true

const slug = 'terms'
const title = 'Terms of Service'
const eyebrow = 'Legal'
const heading = 'Terms of <span class="grad">Service</span>'
const description =
  'The terms that govern your use of the Silkweave website, sign-in, and hosted services. The open-source packages stay under the MIT license.'
const lastUpdated = 'June 26, 2026'

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://www.silkweave.dev' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Terms of Service', item: 'https://www.silkweave.dev/terms' }
  ]
}
---

<PageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  slug={slug}
  eyebrow={eyebrow}
  heading={heading}
  intro="These terms cover the Silkweave website and any hosted service you sign in to. They are not meant to be a wall of fine print, but they do form a binding agreement, so please read them. If you do not agree with them, that is fine, but you should not use the hosted Service."
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {lastUpdated}</p>

  <h2 id="agreement">1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms of Service (the "Terms") are an agreement between you and
    <strong>Atomic BI Pte. Ltd.</strong>, a company incorporated in Singapore ("Atomic", "Silkweave",
    "we", "us"). By signing in to or using the Silkweave website at <code>silkweave.dev</code> and any
    hosted accounts or services linked to it (the "Service"), you agree to these Terms. If you are using
    the Service for an organisation, you confirm you have authority to accept these Terms on its behalf.
  </p>

  <h2 id="open-source">2. The open-source packages are separate</h2>
  <p>
    Silkweave is, first and foremost, an open-source toolkit. The Silkweave packages published on npm and
    GitHub are licensed under the <a href="https://github.com/silkweave/silkweave/blob/master/LICENSE" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MIT
    License</a>, and your rights to use that code come from that license, not from these Terms. These
    Terms govern the hosted website and sign-in only. If anything here ever appears to conflict with the
    MIT License as it applies to the code, the MIT License wins for the code.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <span class="callout-icon">✦</span>
    <p>Short version: install and self-host the libraries however you like under MIT. These Terms only
    kick in when you use our hosted website and sign-in.</p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="accounts">3. Accounts and sign-in</h2>
  <p>
    To use parts of the Service you sign in with a third-party identity provider such as Google or
    GitHub. You are responsible for the account you sign in with and for keeping access to it secure. You
    must be at least 16 years old, and you must give accurate information and keep it current. How we
    handle the data we receive at sign-in is set out in our
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="acceptable-use">4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>When you use the Service, you agree not to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>break the law or infringe anyone else's rights;</li>
    <li>attempt to gain unauthorised access to the Service, other accounts, or our systems;</li>
    <li>probe, scan, overload, or disrupt the Service, or get around its limits and security;</li>
    <li>reverse engineer or misuse the hosted Service (this is separate from your MIT rights to the
      open-source code);</li>
    <li>use the Service to build or train a competing product by scraping or bulk-extracting it; or</li>
    <li>upload anything malicious or unlawful.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="ip">5. Intellectual property and brand</h2>
  <p>
    The source code is yours to use under MIT. The Silkweave name, logo, and the look and content of
    the website are ours (or our licensors'), and nothing here gives you the right to use the Silkweave
