    The Service relies on third parties, including Google and GitHub for sign-in and various
    infrastructure providers for hosting. Your use of those services is also subject to their terms, and
    we are not responsible for them. If a third-party provider changes or removes something we depend on,
    parts of the Service may change too.
  </p>

  <h2 id="availability">7. Changes and availability</h2>
  <p>
    Silkweave is a small, independent project, and we offer the hosted Service on a best-effort basis. We
    may add, change, or remove features, and we may suspend or stop the hosted Service at any time. We
    will try to give reasonable notice of major changes where we can, but we are not obliged to keep any
    particular feature running.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disclaimer">8. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The Service is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranties of any kind, whether express
    or implied, including any implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
    and non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted, error-free, or
    secure. You use it at your own risk, to the fullest extent permitted by law.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, Atomic and its directors and contributors will not be liable
    for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for any loss of data,
